From 40a6c00ba85d7ae2005fbf61ae2127a97bcdb1a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(billing): bill backup storage by volume-priced tiers
 (psa-cvh)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backup cloud usage is already synced onto assets (backup_cloud_bytes) by
the NinjaOne/Comet/Servosity backup syncs, but there was no way to turn
that usage into a billable line — GitHub #125.

This adds a tiered-pricing path through the existing recurring-billing
engine:

- New QuantityType::PerBackupStorageGb. BillingService sums
  backup_cloud_bytes across the contract's assigned assets
  (contract-scoped) or client-wide, then converts bytes -> whole GB with
  the same binary rounding (round(bytes / 1024^3)) the vendor sync uses
  for the cloud_usage_gb license type, so the two measures agree.
- backup_storage_tiers table + BackupStorageTier model: a per-SKU volume
  rate card (up_to_gb inclusive upper bound, null = unbounded catch-all;
  unit_price per GB). Sku::priceForStorageGb() selects the first tier
  that covers the measured GB and bills the whole quantity at that rate.
  Returns null with no tiers so the caller falls back to the flat line
  price; usage above all bounded tiers with no catch-all bills the top
  bounded rate (never an unpriced fallback once tiers exist).
- BillingService::resolveUnitPrice() applies the tier rate in
  generateInvoice() and previewInvoice(), stores it as the invoice line
  unit_price, and annotates quantity_source with the applied rate.
- SKU editor gains a tier rate-card editor (shown when the SKU default
  quantity type is "Backup Storage (GB)"); the profile-line quantity-type
  dropdown picks up the new type automatically. SkuController
  create/update persist tiers transactionally (replace-all, empty rows
  skipped, blank upper bound = unbounded).

No proration and no invoice schema change — the resolved per-GB rate is
stored as the line unit_price, consistent with every other quantity type.

Validation: full suite green (2583 passed); Pint clean on changed files.
